  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Genomics and Science Dojo 3.0: Accelerating Scientific Outputs and Strategic Collaboration with Multisectoral Organisations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Genomics and Science Dojo 3.0 is a six-month capacity-building initiative designed to accelerate scientific productivity, cross-sectoral collaboration, and policy translation in Indonesia&#x2019;s biomedical and genomic research ecosystem. It builds on the success of Dojo 1.0 and 2.0, which trained over 150 scientists and generated more than 30 manuscripts, contributing to the advancement of Indonesia&#x2019;s research and innovation culture. Led by the Summit Institute for Development (SID) in collaboration with OUCRU and GSI, the Dojo 3.0 introduces stronger impact evaluation mechanisms, international collaboration, and sustainability frameworks?. It aims to align with Indonesia&#x2019;s Digital Health Strategy 2025&#x2013;2029, Rencana Induk Bidang Kesehatan (RIBK) priorities on health workforce transformation and research ecosystem strengthening,? and OECD accession in relation to ?open science, evidence-based policymaking, and integrity in research governance.???</narrative>
  </description>
